<activity xml:id="bsoup_writecode2q_v2" label="bsoup_writecode2q_v2">
    <statement>
                 <p>Write a function called <c>headings(soup)</c> that takes a soup object and returns a list of the text from all <c>h2</c> tags in the soup.
                    The soup object is created from the file <c>MOOC-Wikipedia-8-20-2026.html</c> which is a saved version of <q>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massive_open_online_course</q> from 2026. 
      Click on the 
      following link to view the source: <url href="http://web.archive.org/web/20260807063804/https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massive_open_online_course">link</url>

      For example, <c>headings(soup)</c> should return a list of 14 headings starting with <c>['Contents', 'History', 'Equity and access', ...]</c>. 
    </p>
    </statement>
    <program interactive="activecode" language="python3" add-files="MOOC-2026-wikip-id">
        <code>
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup
import requests

def headings(soup):
    # write code here

# read the saved file
fh = open('MOOC-Wikipedia-8-20-2026.html')
text = fh.read()
fh.close()

# create the soup object and print the results
soup = BeautifulSoup(text, 'html.parser')
print(headings(soup))
====
import unittest
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup
import requests

class myTests(unittest.TestCase):

    def testOne(self):
        file = 'MOOC-Wikipedia-8-20-2026.html'
        fh = open(file)
        text = fh.read()
        fh.close()
        soup = BeautifulSoup(text, 'html.parser')
        output = headings(soup)
        self.assertEqual(len(output), 14)
        self.assertEqual(output[0], 'Contents')
        self.assertEqual(output[1], 'History')
        self.assertEqual(output[2], 'Equity and access')
        self.assertEqual(output[3], 'Emergence of MOOC providers')

unittest.main()

        </code>
    </program>
</activity>


